                "entry_id": "1aeb7a02-0f5e-3a1d-952c-7d2a0a7adb90",
                "word": "hypogamy",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e8cfecb8-b469-3f4c-a4e5-f6e2cd975048",
                        "entry_id": "1aeb7a02-0f5e-3a1d-952c-7d2a0a7adb90",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The seeking of a spouse of lower socioeconomic status or caste than oneself."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "26ce2158-b6d5-4d8a-a66c-2ee15034cd13",
                                "sense_id": "e8cfecb8-b469-3f4c-a4e5-f6e2cd975048",
                                "text": "The reverse (hypogamy) is rare because with marriage a woman and her future offspring take on the social position of the husband, and so an upper‐class woman marrying a lower‐class man reduces her position as well as that of her children."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1bd514f0-a13c-42b7-89d2-2dba1d6bfde9",
                                "sense_id": "e8cfecb8-b469-3f4c-a4e5-f6e2cd975048",
                                "text": "Men like Mr. Lim, according to Government officials, often end up marrying \"downward\" - hypogamy - after they fail to win a woman of their own educational level."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
